  "body": "Imagine picking fresh fruit from your own garden, enjoying dinner on the deck, then taking an evening stroll through flowering terraces, with bush and sea views beyond.\r\n\r\nWelcome to 16 Ridgelea Road, Long Bay, where modern family living meets the pleasures of your own garden retreat.\r\n\r\nSet on 5,177sqm of land, more or less, this approx. 431sqm residence offers generous space both inside and out.\r\n\r\nLovingly planted by the owners, the home orchard features a variety of fruit trees, bringing the simple pleasure of homegrown fruit to everyday life.\r\n\r\nWinding pathways connect the landscaped terraces, where a variety of flowers and plantings creates colour and interest. Generous lawns offer room to play and gather, while a decorative pond adds another peaceful feature to this thoughtfully created setting.\r\n\r\nInside, contemporary interiors and large windows connect the home with its surroundings. Bush and sea views unfold from both levels and the living areas, while multiple decks invite you outdoors for morning coffee, relaxed lunches or evenings with friends.\r\n\r\nFour bedrooms, each with its own ensuite, provide comfort and personal space for family and guests. Three living areas offer room to come together or retreat, complemented by a separate study, a kitchen with scullery, two separate toilets and double garaging.\r\n\r\nConvenience complements the peaceful setting. Albany Mega Centre and Westfield Albany are around eight minutes away by car, while Long Bay Town Centre and Regional Park are approx. a 10 minute walk. Pinehurst, Kristin and Massey University are around 10 minutes by car. Zoned for Long Bay School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College, the property also offers easy motorway access towards Auckland’s CBD.\r\n\r\nFor those who love gardening, entertaining and a close connection to nature, this is a home where those pleasures become part of every day.",
